# F8 Auto-Triage (BINDING — no manual re-arm)

The owner is NEVER the bug detector. F8 captures must surface on the CLI without the owner saying "rearm" or "watch".

## One-time per machine (owner or first CLI turn)

Ensure the **persistent daemon** is running (survives forever; auto-rearms on every capture):

```powershell
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .claude\skills\run-defenders\f8-watch-start.ps1
```

Stop only when done for the day: `f8-watch-stop.ps1`.

## Every CLI / Cursor agent session (BINDING)

1. **Session start:** run `f8-watch-start.ps1` (idempotent — no-op if already running).
2. **Session start:** launch **background inbox poll** so mid-session F8s ping the agent without a new user message:
   ```powershell
   powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .claude\skills\run-defenders\f8-watch-poll.ps1
   ```
   Use Shell `is_background: true` + `notify_on_output` pattern `F8 INBOX PING`.
3. **Every turn — FIRST action before any other work:**
   ```powershell
   powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .claude\skills\run-defenders\f8-check-inbox.ps1
   ```
4. **If exit code 0 (`NEW_CAPTURE`):** STOP planned work. Read the file named on the `capture=` line — that is the **OLDEST un-acked** capture (auto-harvested `[Flow:*]` context is inside). `pending=N` tells you how many are queued; `LATEST_CAPTURE.md` only ever holds the NEWEST one. Triage from that data FIRST — no code-read, no theory (§12). Route per `docs/TICKET_PIPELINE.md`.
5. **After triage:** `f8-ack.ps1` — it acks **ONE** capture (the oldest). **Loop back to step 3 until `NO_CAPTURE`**, then **re-launch** background `f8-watch-poll.ps1` (step 2).

## Inbox files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `logs/f8-inbox/QUEUE.jsonl` | **The record** — append-only, one line per capture (WO-965). Nothing is ever overwritten here |
| `logs/f8-inbox/PING.json` | Monotonic seq; producers bump on each capture (a VIEW of the newest) |
| `logs/f8-inbox/LATEST_CAPTURE.md` | Newest capture's harvest + trigger (a VIEW — with a backlog banner when others are queued) |
| `logs/f8-inbox/capture-*-seq<N>.md` | Per-capture harvest, one file per seq — what you actually triage |
| `logs/f8-inbox/ACK.json` | `lastAckSeq` = contiguous watermark + `acked` = out-of-order acks (`f8-ack.ps1`) |
| `logs/f8-inbox/queue-events.log` | Loud ledger: supersede / unqueued / lost / ack events |

**Never assume the newest capture is the only one.** Before WO-965 a burst collapsed into
`LATEST_CAPTURE.md` and a single ack buried the rest — on 2026-08-10 the owner's seq 2307 and 2308
were never surfaced to any seat. Walk `pending=` to zero, every time.

Legacy one-shot watcher `f8-watch.sh` is superseded by daemon + inbox poll unless bash-only environment.